# Agent & Console Patterns

## Chat flow

```
Browser → console /api/chat → commander /chat → router → investigator|orchestrator
```

- Console OIDC (`CONSOLE_AUTH_ENABLED`) is **separate** from inter-agent Bearer auth.
- Chat 401 on `GET /get` = commander missing `agentFetch`, not missing console login.

## Commander outbound calls

All fetches to `INVESTIGATOR_URL`, `ORCHESTRATOR_URL`, `HIL_URL`, `GITOPS_URL`, `SECURITY_URL`, `CICD_URL` must go through `agentFetch()` in `agents/commander/src/agent-fetch.ts`.

External LLM URLs (OpenRouter, Gemini) use plain `fetch`.

## Console proxy

`agents/console/src/server.ts` — `proxyJson()` adds `internalAuthHeaders()`. After helm secret changes, rollout `console-agent`.

## Shared runtime deps

If `shared/src/*.ts` imports an npm package, add it to `shared/package.json` and install shared deps in agent Dockerfiles:

```dockerfile
COPY shared/package*.json ./shared/
RUN cd shared && npm ci --omit=dev
```

## New investigator/orchestrator endpoints

1. Add route in agent `index.ts`
2. If protected: already behind `createInternalAuthMiddleware`
3. Wire commander caller with `agentFetch`
4. Add E2E smoke in `scripts/test-e2e-kind.sh` or `test-e2e-advanced-features.sh`
5. Document env vars in `helm/sre-bot/values.yaml` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` if user-facing
